{
  "dom_id": "step-q352755",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Suppose that\n\n$$\nS={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{(-2)}^{n}}{(n+1)!}\n$$\n\nand that ${s}_{5}$ is the fifth partial sum of $S.$ According to the alternating series error bound, $|S-{s}_{5}|<k$ for some real number $k.$ Find the value of $k.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{2}^{n}}{(n+1)!}$ and ${b}_{n}=\\frac{{(-2)}^{n}}{(n+1)!}.$ Then ${a}_{n}$ is positive and decreasing for $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ So, the series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\nBecause our series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $5$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{5}|<|{b}_{6}|=|\\frac{{(-2)}^{6}}{(6+1)!}|=\\frac{64}{5040}=\\frac{4}{315}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\frac{4}{315}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
